# Local agent tooling and working docs.
# These drive Cline in this checkout; they are not part of the deployed site,
# so they stay local instead of being pushed to GitHub Pages.
docs/
.clinerules/
.cline/skills/
.clineignore
README.txt

# The test suite, untracked at the reader's request.
#
# THE TRADE, STATED PLAINLY: smoke.mjs alone is 190KB and the mutation script is
# 33KB, and neither is reachable from the deployed page - they are development
# machinery. But they are also the suite that proves the claims this page makes,
# and the commit history for them is most of the project's record.
#
# So after this, a fresh clone cannot run `npm run verify`: package.json still
# has the scripts and the files will not be there. They remain on this machine,
# which is where the work happens.
tools/

# Local environment files. Commit a .env.example with empty values if a
# template is useful, but never the real thing.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build and coverage output. This project has no build step and no
# dependencies, so none of this can be produced by `npm run` - but a stray
# dist/ or a coverage report from an unrelated tool should never reach Pages.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# The page the pixel test assembles from index.html + pixel-probe.html. It is
# rewritten on every run and removed afterwards, so it should never be staged.
.pixel-run.html
